<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Nice</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Nikaia</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Nice is a city on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mediterranean">Mediterranean</a> coast of south-eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> and capital of the Alpes-Maritimes <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/departement">department</a>. It began as Nikaia, a Greek trading post founded by Massalia, while the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roman-empire">Romans</a> built <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cemenelum">Cemenelum</a> on the hill above. For most of the period from 1388 to 1860 it belonged to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/house-of-savoy">House of Savoy</a>, before being ceded to France in 1860, and it became a leading resort of the Riviera.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/nice.jpg" alt="Nice" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Alexander Migl · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Promenade_des_Anglais_Nice_IMG_1255.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
